    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"untamed by the ravages of time\"... that's a powerful way to put it. it sounds almost like he's winning by leaving. \n\nit's just hard to stay objective about it because the more i write about aris, the more i feel that same fear in myself. the fear that everything i am right now is already starting to slip away, and that if i just keep going, i'll eventually just be a hollow version of the person i used to be. \n\nif i were to write it so that his choice wasn't an act of despair, but an act of preservation... like he's protecting his soul from being worn down by the world... do you think that makes it a more profound ending? that he's choosing the end to keep his dignity intact?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
